</span></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1. </span>Dataset statistics for code completion tasks across three programming languages: Python, Csharp, and Java. The “25% Quartile" indicates that 25% of the code sequences in the dataset have a length shorter than the reported value. The “50% Quartile," also known as the median, is the midpoint, where half of the code sequences are shorter, and half are longer. The “75% Quartile" marks the point below which 75% of the code sequences fall, representing the upper quartile.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Large Language Models (LLMs)</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2024a)</a></cite>, we have considered RoPE-based LLMs such as LLaMA-2 (7B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, Sheared-LLaMA (1.3B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, TinyLlama (1.1B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>, Vicuna (7B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> to conduct zero-shot inference in a low-resource scenario.
The detailed model statistics is presented in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2. Large Language Models (LLMs) ‣ 4. Experimental Setup ‣ An Evaluation of Context Length Extrapolation in Long Code via Positional Embeddings and Efficient Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:69.7pt;vertical-align:-32.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(18.1pt,-3.7pt) scale(1.11701243124124,1.11701243124124) ;">
